IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fa-2006-maternity`

-- A New Tax System (Family Assistance) Act 1999 as in force on 30 August 2006 (C2006C00402) -- worked cases for
-- fa-2006-maternity.l4 (REQ-0062, 22 October 2026).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected results were written by hand
-- from ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00490.2006-07-01.txt.
--
-- The life: Jake, k002 (event dated 2006-10-01). Jake was born on 30 August 2006 to Graham (36) and Sue (33), a couple in
-- Perth; Chloe, born 14 March 2003, is the older child. The family's income is not stated. ASSUMED: Sue is eligible for
-- Family Tax Benefit for Jake within 13 weeks of the birth (or would be but for a nil rate), as a parent in a couple on any
-- income is at least that; Graham would also be eligible, and the Secretary determines Sue is the one (s 37(2)). The FTB
-- dollar figures used are the ones printed in the compilation, which are labelled examples and not the 2006-07 rates.

`Sue, for Jake (k002)` MEANS `My new child` WITH
    `how`                                                   IS `I am a parent of the child, born alive`
    `born on`                                               IS 20060830
    `FTB eligible for the child within 13 weeks, or would be but for a nil rate` IS TRUE
    `entrusted to me or my partner within 13 weeks of the birth` IS FALSE
    `likely to stay in that care for at least 13 weeks`     IS FALSE
    `entrusted by an authorised party, aged under 2`        IS FALSE
    `if from overseas, under 2 on arriving in Australia`    IS FALSE
    `another individual would also be eligible`             IS TRUE
    `the Secretary determined that I am eligible`           IS TRUE
    `my percentage under a section 37(3) determination`     IS 100

