§ `ss 36, 37 -- eligibility`

-- k002: Sue, a parent eligible for FTB for Jake within 13 weeks, chosen by the Secretary under s 37(2): eligible. Graham,
-- not chosen: not eligible (s 37(1), only one). No FTB eligibility within 13 weeks: not eligible. A non-parent given care
-- within 13 weeks for at least 13 weeks: eligible (s 36(3)); for 6 weeks: not. An adoption of a child aged 3: not (s
-- 36(5)(b)). A stillborn child: eligible (s 36(4)).
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the maternity payment` `Sue, for Jake (k002)`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible for the maternity payment` `Graham, for Jake, not the one the Secretary chose (k002)`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible for the maternity payment` `a parent not eligible for FTB within 13 weeks`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the maternity payment` `a grandparent given care of a newborn for at least 13 weeks`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible for the maternity payment` `a carer for only 6 weeks`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I eligible for the maternity payment` `an adoption of a child aged 3`
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the maternity payment` `a stillborn child, July 2006`

§ `s 66 -- the amount`

-- s 66(1) "$4,000", in force from 1 July 2006; MAT is next indexed on 20 September 2006 (Schedule 4 cl 3, item 17A). 30
-- August 2006: $4,000. 19 September 2006: $4,000. 20 September 2006 and 30 June 2006: not in the deposited text.
#ASSERT `the maternity payment amount in force on` 20060830 EQUALS `dollars` 4000
#ASSERT `the maternity payment amount in force on` 20060919 EQUALS `dollars` 4000
#ASSERT `the maternity payment amount in force on` 20060920 EQUALS `not covered: the indexed figure for that day is not in the deposited text`
#ASSERT `the maternity payment amount in force on` 20060630 EQUALS `not covered: the indexed figure for that day is not in the deposited text`

-- k002: Sue gets $4,000 for Jake. Graham: not eligible. A 50% share under s 37(3): $2,000 (s 66(2)). A birth on 25 September
-- 2006: eligible, but the indexed amount is not in the deposit.
#ASSERT `How much maternity payment do I get` `Sue, for Jake (k002)` EQUALS `dollars` 4000
#ASSERT `How much maternity payment do I get` `Graham, for Jake, not the one the Secretary chose (k002)` EQUALS `not eligible`
#ASSERT `How much maternity payment do I get` `a share of 50% set under section 37(3)` EQUALS `dollars` 2000
#ASSERT `How much maternity payment do I get` `a birth on 25 September 2006, after the indexation day` EQUALS `not covered: the indexed figure for that day is not in the deposited text`

§ `Schedule 1 -- what Jake added to Family Tax Benefit`

-- k002, on the printed figures (labelled examples, not the 2006-07 rates): Jake, a second FTB child under 13, adds $2,920.00
-- (cl 7 item 1) + $600 (cl 38A) = $3,520 a year to the maximum rate of Part A, and raises the higher income free area by
-- $3,000 (cl 2). A third child, or a multiple birth: not covered. A first child adds no HIFA.
#ASSERT `What a new child under 13 adds to my maximum Part A rate` `the rates as printed in C2006C00402` 1 FALSE EQUALS `dollars` 3520
#ASSERT `What a new child under 13 adds to my maximum Part A rate` `the rates as printed in C2006C00402` 0 FALSE EQUALS `dollars` 3520
#ASSERT `What a new child under 13 adds to my maximum Part A rate` `the rates as printed in C2006C00402` 2 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: a third FTB child or a multiple birth (large family supplement, multiple birth allowance)`
#ASSERT `What a new child under 13 adds to my maximum Part A rate` `the rates as printed in C2006C00402` 1 TRUE EQUALS `not covered: a third FTB child or a multiple birth (large family supplement, multiple birth allowance)`
#ASSERT `How much a new child raises my higher income free area` `the rates as printed in C2006C00402` 1 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `How much a new child raises my higher income free area` `the rates as printed in C2006C00402` 0 EQUALS 0

-- k002: Chloe was 3, so the youngest FTB child was already under 5: Part B's standard rate does not change. Were the older
-- child 6: 2,569.60 - 1,781.20 = 788.40. A first child: the full 2,569.60.
#ASSERT `How much a new child changes my Part B standard rate` `the rates as printed in C2006C00402` 1 3 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much a new child changes my Part B standard rate` `the rates as printed in C2006C00402` 1 6 EQUALS 788.40
#ASSERT `How much a new child changes my Part B standard rate` `the rates as printed in C2006C00402` 0 0 EQUALS 2569.60
